  "body": "There is a scattering of discussion about UX and security concerns in a few different issues. (#29, #27, and again in #35) I recomend reading the [\"Security Considerations\"](https://github.com/whatwg/serial/blob/7edd88b59b7525add223633bcbcc46891dce6d09/index.html#L272) passage from #27.\n\nConcerns that have been raised are\n- Flashing hardware and subsequently getting it past the mozilla security team, \"It will be hard for me to champion this internally unless we, as community, can argue that this won't brick any devices.\" - @marcoscaceres \n- Identifying uses based upon what devices they have plugged in\n- Malicious web sites accesses devices they shouldn't\n- Blacklisting devices based upon VID/PID combos\n- HTTPS only\n\nI'll keep this list up to date and add any new concerns and link to their discussions.\n",
